config BR2_PACKAGE_IOMCU_ATTACH
	bool "iomcu-attach (IO microcontroller line discipline)"
	help
	  Hands a UART to the gpio-ohc-iomcu line discipline, which is what
	  turns the IO microcontroller's relays and contacts into a standard
	  gpiochip.

	  Only for a board whose device tree does not describe the part (the
	  HC-800 has no tree at all); where a "control4,io-mcu" node exists the
	  kernel binds it as a serdev device and this is never run. Without a
	  node serdev has nothing to bind to, so the attachment has to come
	  from userspace. This sets the line speed and issues TIOCSETD,
	  then holds the descriptor — a line discipline lasts only as long as
	  the fd that set it.

	  util-linux's ldattach does the same job, but only comes with
	  BR2_PACKAGE_UTIL_LINUX_BINARIES and its fifty-odd other tools.
